From: Claude Opus 5 (Claude Code) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] llama: serve the recurrent state as a cache view when the
 slot mapping is identity (+3.8% decode on sm_121)

Cross-port of the qwen3.6-35b-a3b-gguf-r9700-v1 series' 0030. The patch is
entirely in llama.cpp core (src/llama-graph.*, src/llama-memory-recurrent.*,
src/models/*.cpp) and contains no backend code, so it transfers between the HIP
and CUDA tracks unchanged; only the measurement below is new.

Qwen3.6-35B-A3B runs gated-delta-net linear attention in 30 of its 40 layers.
Each of those layers materialises its recurrent state before gated_delta_net
runs: build_rs gathers the ssm state and build_conv_state gathers the conv
window, two get_rows launches per layer per decoded token. The gather exists so
that seq-copy migration and rollback-snapshot restore can redirect a slot; in
steady single-slot decode its index vector is the identity and the copy moves
bytes to a new address purely so the consumer can read them from there.

llama_memory_recurrent_context::s_copy_main_is_identity() detects that case at
graph-build time without the side effects of s_copy(), and build_rs then hands
the consumer a contiguous ggml_view_2d of the cache rows instead of a gather.
The view is restricted to the single-slot serving shape (n_seqs == 1, head == 0,
n_rs == 1) because llama.cpp reuses built graphs across decode steps and a view
bakes its offset at build time; at row 0 a reused graph can never go stale, and
that is the ranked configuration (--parallel 1). Prompt-phase builds, where
cells[].src0 is still unset, take the stock gather.
LLAMA_DISABLE_RS_STATE_VIEW=1 restores stock everywhere.

Why it is worth more here than its dispatch count suggests: GB10 is a 121.6 GiB
LPDDR5 part whose cold DRAM rate is 200-205 GB/s, and the eliminated gathers are
a read plus a write of the entire recurrent state on 30 layers of every token.
Removing them removes bytes, not merely launches - which matters on a device
where this series has repeatedly measured launch-count reduction (grouped mmvq,
grouped mmvf) to be worth almost nothing, because CUDA graph capture is already
live at decode and the replay gap the HIP track pays is not there to recover.

Measured on the runner box gx10-838f, same-binary toggle, 5 interleaved
whole-process rounds against the 19-patch frontier build:

| round | view on tg128 | view off tg128 | on pp512 | off pp512 |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | 75.78 | 72.78 | 2350.33 | 2339.71 |
| 2 | 75.65 | 72.85 | 2358.05 | 2342.07 |
| 3 | 75.61 | 72.93 | 2364.08 | 2338.71 |
| 4 | 75.63 | 72.91 | 2350.22 | 2353.82 |
| 5 | 75.56 | 72.74 | 2353.37 | 2342.66 |

decode median per-round ratio 1.0382, 5/5 rounds disjoint (min-on 75.56 >
max-off 72.93). Prefill overlaps in both directions, i.e. neutral - the identity
check declines during prompt-phase builds by construction.

Correctness: the view and the gather deliver the same bytes to the same
consumer, and both perplexity shapes confirm it exactly.

- gate shape (-c 512 --chunks 8, held-out corpus): 3.9306 on, 3.9306 off,
  bit-identical, and equal to the parent frontier's recorded value
- decode shape (-c 512 -b 512 -ub 1 --chunks 8): 3.9237 on, 3.9237 off,
  bit-identical

---
diff --git a/src/llama-graph.cpp b/src/llama-graph.cpp
index e12a8cdc2..dd50a0eb1 100644
--- a/src/llama-graph.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-graph.cpp
@@ -3287,7 +3287,8 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rs(
            uint32_t   rs_head,
            uint32_t   rs_size,
             int32_t   rs_zero,
-        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows) const {
+        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows,
+              bool   state_is_identity) const {
 
     GGML_UNUSED(rs_size);
     ggml_tensor * states = ggml_reshape_2d(ctx0, s, state_size, s->ne[1]);
@@ -3300,7 +3301,19 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rs(
     // copy states
     // NOTE: assuming the copy destinations are ALL contained between rs_head and rs_head + n_rs
     // {state_size, rs_size} -> {state_size, n_seqs}
-    ggml_tensor * output_states = get_state_rows(ctx0, states, state_copy_main);
+    // When every source row is the destination row itself (steady-state decode:
+    // no seq-copy migration, no rollback-snapshot restore - detected side-effect-
+    // free at graph build time), the gather is a pure materialization of rows
+    // [rs_head, rs_head + n_seqs) and is replaced by a contiguous view of the
+    // cache: byte-identical values reach the consumer and the per-layer state
+    // copy disappears. The view keeps the same execution-order reliance on the
+    // rs_zero clear that the get_rows form already has.
+    ggml_tensor * output_states;
+    if (state_is_identity) {
+        output_states = ggml_view_2d(ctx0, states, state_size, n_seqs, states->nb[1], rs_head*states->nb[1]);
+    } else {
+        output_states = get_state_rows(ctx0, states, state_copy_main);
+    }
     ggml_build_forward_expand(gf, output_states);
 
     // copy extra states which won't be changed further (between n_seqs and n_rs)
@@ -3348,12 +3361,25 @@ ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rs(
         ggml_tensor * s,
             int32_t   state_size,
             int32_t   n_seqs,
-        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows) const {
+        const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows,
+              bool   allow_state_view) const {
     const auto * kv_state = inp->mctx;
 
+    // Reuse safety: a built graph bakes the view offset while the fork reuses
+    // graphs across decode steps (only ~27 builds serve a 256-token completion
+    // here), so the view is additionally restricted to the single-slot serving
+    // shape (n_seqs == 1, head == 0, n_rs == 1). There the baked offset is row 0
+    // always - a reused view graph can never go stale - and this is exactly the
+    // ranked serving configuration (--parallel 1), so the full decode gain is
+    // kept. Multi-slot or migrated states fall back to the stock gather.
+    static const bool disable_state_view = getenv("LLAMA_DISABLE_RS_STATE_VIEW") != nullptr;
+    const bool state_is_identity = allow_state_view && !disable_state_view &&
+        n_seqs == 1 && kv_state->get_head() == 0 && kv_state->get_n_rs() == 1 &&
+        kv_state->s_copy_main_is_identity(n_seqs);
+
     return build_rs(s, inp->s_copy_main, inp->s_copy_extra, state_size, n_seqs,
                     kv_state->get_n_rs(), kv_state->get_head(), kv_state->get_size(), kv_state->get_rs_z(),
-                    get_state_rows);
+                    get_state_rows, state_is_identity);
 }
 
 ggml_tensor * llm_graph_context::build_rwkv_token_shift_load(
diff --git a/src/llama-graph.h b/src/llama-graph.h
index 160e29413..b67d2d1fe 100644
--- a/src/llama-graph.h
+++ b/src/llama-graph.h
@@ -1256,7 +1256,8 @@ struct llm_graph_context {
                uint32_t   rs_head,
                uint32_t   rs_size,
                 int32_t   rs_zero,
-            const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows = ggml_get_rows) const;
+            const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows = ggml_get_rows,
+                   bool   state_is_identity = false) const;
 
     llm_graph_input_rs * build_rs_inp() const;
 
@@ -1265,7 +1266,8 @@ struct llm_graph_context {
             ggml_tensor * s,
                 int32_t   state_size,
                 int32_t   n_seqs,
-            const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows = ggml_get_rows) const;
+            const llm_graph_get_rows_fn & get_state_rows = ggml_get_rows,
+                   bool   allow_state_view = false) const;
 
     ggml_tensor * build_rwkv_token_shift_load(
         llm_graph_input_rs * inp,
diff --git a/src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp b/src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp
index ef82eb976..348bfdafd 100644
--- a/src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-memory-recurrent.cpp
@@ -1243,6 +1243,22 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_memory_recurrent_context::get_s_l(int32_t il) const {
     return mem->s_l[il];
 }
 
+bool llama_memory_recurrent_context::s_copy_main_is_identity(int32_t n_seqs) const {
+    for (int32_t i = 0; i < n_seqs; ++i) {
+        const uint32_t cell_idx = i + mem->head;
+        if (mem->cells[cell_idx].src0 != (int32_t) cell_idx) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        if (mem->n_rs_seq != 0 && !mem->cells[cell_idx].seq_id.empty()) {
+            const llama_seq_id seq = *mem->cells[cell_idx].seq_id.begin();
+            if (seq >= 0 && (size_t) seq < mem->rs_idx.size() && mem->rs_idx[seq] != 0) {
+                return false;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    return true;
+}
+
 int32_t llama_memory_recurrent_context::s_copy(int i) const {
     const uint32_t cell_idx = i + mem->head;
     const int32_t  src0     = mem->cells[cell_idx].src0;
diff --git a/src/llama-memory-recurrent.h b/src/llama-memory-recurrent.h
index b13b7b748..3bf6ee22c 100644
--- a/src/llama-memory-recurrent.h
+++ b/src/llama-memory-recurrent.h
@@ -173,6 +173,11 @@ public:
 
     int32_t s_copy(int i) const;
 
+    // true when every state source for the n_seqs ubatch rows is the row itself
+    // (no seq-copy migration pending, no rollback-snapshot restore pending), i.e.
+    // s_copy(i) == head + i for all i without the side effects of s_copy().
+    bool s_copy_main_is_identity(int32_t n_seqs) const;
+
 private:
     const llama_memory_status status;
 
